<title>USA: Mail-Well stake cut by Vinik to 4.7 pct.</title>
<headline>Mail-Well stake cut by Vinik to 4.7 pct.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-04-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>A group led by Boston investor Jeffrey Vinik said Wednesday it has reduced its stake in Mail-Well Inc to 582,100 shares, or 4.7 percent, from 806,400 shares, or 6.5 percent.</p>
<p>In a filing with the U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission, the group said it most recently sold a net 224,300 common shares between March 11 and April 1 at prices ranging from $18.92 to $20.82 a share.</p>
